# Cast for his mana cost, Leonardo enters untapped and not attacking: sneak's "enters tapped and attacking" is only for a
# spell whose sneak cost was paid (CR 702.190b). Sneak is refused in a main phase (CR 702.190a). On turn 5 he attacks with
# Healer's Hawk; each lifelinker's combat damage is its own life-gaining event (CR 120.3f, 702.15b; the ruling), so "whenever
# you gain life" triggers twice and he gets two +1/+1 counters: Bot1 at 22, Bot2 at 18, Leonardo a 3/3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Healer's Hawk
Leonardo, Cutting Edge
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Healer's Hawk.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
! Bot1.Hand.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Cast(Ability: Sneak)
Bot1.Hand.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.SummoningSick = true
? Combat.Attackers.Count = 0
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Leonardo, Cutting Edge > Bot2; Healer's Hawk > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Toughness = 3
